Z||000007||1FST2M6||11-30-2000||09:34 AM||||yeah i can make about anything.. but.. not sure that it'll be cost effective.. <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A>  has poly mounts.. and they (in the car i installed them in) rattle your eyeballs. and solid ones would be worse. i had solid mounts in my old 79 Corvette for less than a weekend... just new stock ones were a sweet improvement with ultimate dog bone. from either Cwestco or the fiero store. <P>and uum ALL of our cars act strange with lots of torque.. i had 310lbft at the wheels in my SE under nitrous (at the track) and it had NASTY wheels hop, the bushings would crush and split and the a-arms can fold. (Koni, eibachs and bar)  I've been trying to get a set of Chris Wests rear bushing replacements to needle bearings but he won't pony up. i wanted a set when i bought my headers. I'll e-mail him again...   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000008||theogre||11-30-2000||09:25 PM||||I put a polly cradle set in mine. the things are about as hard as rocks. It was amazing how much tighter the car was after putting them in. The poly doesn't need any greasing in this application. the bushings don't move like A arms do so there's nothing to make them squeak. Mine are in with no grease at all.||||reg||1
